      "Access is the right to be told what is going on with your data. Section 11 says the Data Principal may obtain from the Data Fiduciary a summary of the personal data being processed and the processing activities undertaken. She may also obtain the identities of other Data Fiduciaries and Data Processors with whom the data was shared, plus a description of the personal data shared, and any other prescribed information. A clothing site that can say 'we hold your size and address, we use them to fulfil orders, and we shared the address with this courier' is speaking the shape of the right. The section commences on 13 May 2027.",
